    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-31",
      "problem": "The figure below shows the graph of $f(x).$ Determine $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 2} \\left(\\dfrac{2-7x}{xf(x)+2}\\right)^3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14198442/assets/5059a2cee34ad8547bf1af6239ab4a8356e715cd920707cf5f33d2de105a5c1d.png)",
      "worked_solution": "From the graph, we find $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 2} f(x)=3.$ Therefore, using the power rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}{(\\frac{2-7x}{xf(x)+2})}^{3} & ={({lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{2-7x}{xf(x)+2})}^{3} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2-7(2)}{(2\\cdot 3)+2})}^{3} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{-12}{8})}^{3} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{-3}{2})}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{27}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
